<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alaungpaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1714">1714</a>–<a href="/years/1760">1760</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Aung Zeya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alaungpaya was the founder of the Konbaung dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, reigning from 1752 to 1760. Born Aung Zeya, a headman of the village of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shwebo">Moksobo</a>, he resisted the Restored Hanthawaddy kingdom after its capture of Ava, made Moksobo his capital as Shwebo and reunified Burma within a few years. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a> in 1755 and died during a campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in Siam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alaungpaya.jpg" alt="Alaungpaya" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Phyo WP · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alaungpaya.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
